# Brand / UI Rules

## Emotional mode
The visual language must feel:
- calm
- safe
- structured
- human
- professional
- non-judgmental

Avoid:
- aggressive marketing tone
- cold sterile medical look
- visual pressure
- decorative chaos
- overly dark interface
- flashy CTA styling

## Typography
Locked typography pair:
- Headings: Manrope
- Body / UI: Inter

Do not replace with random alternatives.

## Color hierarchy
Locked hierarchy:
- green-first
- blue-second
- light warm / soft neutral backgrounds
- warning color only functional

## Brand colors
- Primary Green: #2E8B3C
- Deep Green: #1F5E2A
- Support Blue: #3F6EA8
- Deep Blue: #2F496B
- Warm Background: #F8F7F3
- Soft Neutral: #F2F6F4
- Text Primary: #24312B
- Text Secondary: #5F6E67
- Border: #D8E2DC
- Hope Accent: #D7A85B
- Warning Accent: #B5544F

## Warning rule
#B5544F may be used only for:
- error
- warning
- urgency micro-accent

Do not use it for:
- primary CTA
- hero emphasis
- large backgrounds
- dominant visual sections

## UI hierarchy
- Primary CTA = green
- Secondary/info actions = blue
- Footer = deep green
- Forms = clean, low-noise, trust-focused
- Cards = soft, restrained, non-glossy
- Sticky contact bar = unified, simple, not multicolor chaos

## Print rule
Use one brand system for:
- web
- print

Allow print-safe adaptation, but do not invent a separate brand system.